    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d172">

                <pb facs="0167" n="155" xml:id="pg155"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.5018/6: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Iran</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-08-29T17:00:00-04:00">August 29, 1942—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>227. Your 271, August 26. Department approves your recommendation and authorizes
                    you to join British in insisting that Iranians take all possible steps to effect
                    efficient control and distribution of domestic wheat supplies before requesting
                    further imports.</p>
                <p>In taking this action we have in mind imminent departure of Sheridan,<anchor
                        n="43" xml:id="d172-f1"/> who should be of great assistance in straightening
                    out internal organization.</p>
                <p>Kidd,<anchor n="44" xml:id="d172-f2"/> who should be able to help with work of
                    transport board, was to leave London August 27 for Tehran via Cairo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d172-f1" n="43" xml:id="d172-f1-content">
                <p>J. P. Sheridan, appointed as Food and Supply Adviser to the Iranian
                    Government.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d172-f2" n="44" xml:id="d172-f2-content">
                <p>Philip Kidd, Lend-Lease representative in Iran.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
